[h1]Speculative Markets[/h1]
Victoria 3's economy gets a financial system. Investors chase rising prices, banks lend into the boom, and when confidence breaks, a panic can leave your factories paying off bad loans for years. Every country also gets a stock Exchange that competes with the rest of the world.

You steer the cycle through credit policy, interventions in hot or cold goods, bank rescues and your laws.

Version [b]__VERSION__[/b], built for [b]Victoria 3 1.15.2[/b]. Supports running campaigns and saves from earlier versions.

[h1]Features[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Market Confidence[/b] from Panic to Mania, moved by booms, crashes, debt and wars.
[*][b]Investor Interest[/b] in every traded good, across nine market sectors.
[*][b]Speculative bubbles[/b] that build in a mania and burst when the mood turns.
[*][b]Financial Panics[/b] that call in loans, cut construction and leave Bad Debts.
[*][b]Bank credit[/b] with leverage, lending standards and a credit policy you set.
[*][b]A stock Exchange for every country[/b] with Standing, Trust, a charter and Specialities.
[*][b]Blue chip companies[/b] that steady the market.
[*][b]Rival Exchanges[/b] with world rankings, contests and moves against each other.
[*][b]Contagion[/b] that can turn a Great Power's panic into a worldwide Long Depression.
[*][b]Politics[/b] with interest group stances on goods, a Monetary Standard and Financial Integration.
[/list]

Open [b]Finance[/b] on the left sidebar. Hover over almost any figure to see how it is calculated. The [url=https://claude.ai/artifact/RK4Lrf6U1rU7HC8Vx5pDvy][b]interactive tutorial[/b][/url] lets you try the levers before you play.

[h1]The cycle[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/AQJqgii.png[/img]
Rising prices make investors keen, and a keen market lifts confidence. Banks lend more freely, and the credit speeds up construction. Above 80 confidence the market is in a Mania, and [b]Speculative Excess[/b] builds up.

When the mood turns, the bubble pops. If confidence falls below your Panic Threshold, a [b]Financial Panic[/b] begins. Banks call in loans, output and taxes fall, and private construction is cut. What the banks cannot cover becomes [b]Bad Debts[/b], a drag on output for years. The more you borrowed, the worse the fall.

[h1]Trading Floor[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/YUCFqBJ.jpeg[/img]
Your Exchange grows from Provincial to National and International Standing. The world's top three are [b]World Centres[/b]. Its [b]Trust[/b] rises in steady years and falls after panics.

Choose a charter. A [b]Commodity Exchange[/b] makes booms stronger, a [b]Money Market[/b] protects Trust, and a [b]Share Market[/b] allows more credit. Higher Standing opens [b]Specialities[/b] such as Futures Pit and Railway Mania. Each is a [b]Path to Renown[/b], a race against every Exchange that pursues it. The top places pay more, but every path has a drawback.

A company that stays prosperous for a year becomes a [b]blue chip[/b]. Blue chips soften crashes, add Trust, raise investment and pull contests your way.

[h1]Speculation[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/4XY1pZN.png[/img]
[b]Market Confidence[/b] runs from 0 to 100. See what moved it, what a sharp fall would cost, and what the market is doing to investment, GDP, construction and trade.

Each good has its own [b]Investor Interest[/b], from Fleeing to Feverish. Hot goods earn their makers more, then end harder. After a long run of high or low prices, investors may [b]favor[/b] or [b]shun[/b] a good for a year.

[b]Restrain[/b] a hot good or [b]Encourage[/b] a cold one with Authority. A [b]Great Issue[/b] raises your Exchange score but puts Trust at risk.

[h1]Banking[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/1FU4JRZ.png[/img]
Each month of [b]Credit Leverage[/b] adds 3.5% throughput, up to 14%. Past three months, panics come sooner, last longer and cut deeper.

Set [b]Credit Policy[/b] to Tight, Normal or Loose. [b]Lending Standards[/b] drift from Strict toward Reckless in good times. Looser banks lend more, but a panic calls in more of the debt.

In a panic, [b]Lend to the Banks[/b] to shorten it. Pledge a cheaper rescue in advance, or buy up bad loans afterwards.

[h1]Exchanges[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/2WhEHpI.png[/img]
Every Exchange at National Standing or above is ranked. The top five gain prestige and a higher Lending Limit.

Name a competitor from the rankings or the map. A contest settles after five years, and a decisive win draws capital from the loser for a year. Push with a [b]Bear Raid[/b], [b]Lure Their Capital[/b] or a [b]Press Campaign[/b]. Defend with [b]Hold the Line[/b] or [b]Shore Up[/b].

[h1]Panics abroad[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/hvBjAnr.jpeg[/img]
A Great Power's panic spreads through trade and foreign ownership. From around 1870 it can grow into a worldwide [b]Long Depression[/b]. The Financial Markets journal entry opens a map of every country's market.

[h1]Politics and laws[/h1]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/3hceafU.jpeg[/img]
Each [b]interest group[/b] supports about two goods and may oppose one. Booms, busts and your interventions in them move its approval.

The [b]Monetary Standard[/b] law group adds Bimetallism, the Gold Standard and Fiat Money. Each changes how booms, panics and rescues play out.

Power blocs can adopt [b]Financial Integration[/b] to shelter members from each other's panics and share the leader's credit.

Economic system and trade laws and the finance technologies also shape the markets. Speculation stops under Command Economy or Cooperative Ownership.

[h1]Alerts, news and rules[/h1]
Alerts warn of an approaching panic or a growing bubble. A monthly bulletin groups market news by sector. Events for manias, panics and depressions let you choose a response. The [b]Market Volatility[/b] game rule has a High setting.

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
This mod changes the top bar, alert row, sidebar, goods panel, interest group panel and building definitions. Mods that replace those, including The Great Rework, may need a patch.
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275348]CMF patch[/url], loaded last.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839705018]Morgenroete patch[/url].
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3841713072]Tech & Res patch[/url], which also covers Morgenroete.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3844392018]Better Politics Mod patch[/url], loaded after Better Politics Mod and Speculative Markets.
[/list]
[b]CMF > Morgenroete > Speculative Markets > Morgenroete patch > CMF patch[/b]
[b]CMF > Tech & Res > Speculative Markets > Tech & Res patch > CMF patch[/b]

For multiplayer, everyone needs the mod. Available in 11 languages, machine assisted.

Try updates early on the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275304]Beta[/url]. [b]Enable only one of the two.[/b]

For bug reports, include versions, other mods and what happened.

